IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nsw-wc-core`

-- Workers Compensation Act 1987 (NSW), with the 1998 Act and the 2016 Regulation -- from the seat of the injured worker
-- (and, on the worker's death, the worker's dependants).
--
-- SEAT: the worker the Acts compensate. "How much is my weekly payment this week, and when does it step down or stop?
-- Can I keep payments after week 130 or 260, and after pension age? How long will my medical expenses be paid? What lump
-- sum is payable for my impairment? What must I do, and by when, to keep my entitlement? Has the insurer or my employer
-- missed a deadline?" The questions under "If the worker has died" are asked by the dependants. The rules are in
-- nsw-wc-core.l4; this module restates none and keeps its own names (none shared with nsw-wc-seat-insurer.l4 or
-- nsw-wc-seat-employer.l4). Judgments the Acts give to the insurer, a medical assessor or the Commission are asked as
-- facts. Every indexed amount is asked as the declared figure if the worker knows it; left empty, the figure in the
-- deposited text is used (it is out of date: see NOTES.md).
--
-- Edition: the Open Australian Legal Corpus texts as at 10 March 2025 (1987 Act version 2023-10-30, 1998 Act version
-- 2024-07-01, Regulation version 2024-07-24) -- not the current official text, and possibly out of date.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workers Compensation Act 1987 (NSW) -- the injured worker's questions`

§§ `My earnings (Schedule 3; Regulation cl 8AB; s 82A)`

@export What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings (1987 Act Schedule 3 cl 2; Regulation cl 8AB minimum of $155)?
GIVEN `my gross earnings in the relevant earning period` IS A NUMBER @desc Your gross earnings, in dollars, for work in every employment you had when injured, over the 52 weeks before the injury (as the Regulation adjusts that period)
      `the weeks in my relevant earning period` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of weeks in that period: 52, unless Regulation Part 4 Division 2 shortens or aligns it (for example, you started the job later, or took unpaid leave)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings` MEANS
    `the pre-injury average weekly earnings` `my gross earnings in the relevant earning period` `the weeks in my relevant earning period`

@export What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings after a review date, 1 April or 1 October (1987 Act ss 82A, 82C)?
GIVEN `my pre-injury average weekly earnings as last varied` IS A NUMBER @desc Your pre-injury average weekly earnings, in dollars, as last varied (or as first worked out, before any review date)
      `the factor declared for the review date` IS A NUMBER @desc The factor the State Insurance Regulatory Authority declared by order for this review date under s 82A(4) (for example 1.02)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings after the review date` MEANS
    `the earnings varied on the review date` `my pre-injury average weekly earnings as last varied` `the factor declared for the review date`

@export What are my current weekly earnings this week (1987 Act Schedule 3 cl 8)?
GIVEN `my actual gross earnings this week` IS A NUMBER @desc What you actually earned this week, gross, in dollars (0 if nothing)
      `what I am able to earn a week in suitable employment` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly amount you are able to earn in suitable employment, in dollars, as assessed (0 if you have no current work capacity)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What are my current weekly earnings` MEANS
    `the current weekly earnings` `my actual gross earnings this week` `what I am able to earn a week in suitable employment`

§§ `My impairment and my needs (s 32A)`

@export Am I a worker with high needs (1987 Act s 32A)?
GIVEN `my injury has resulted in permanent impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury has left you with some permanent impairment
      `my impairment has been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the degree of your permanent impairment has been assessed (under s 65, for Division 4)
      `my assessed degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc The assessed degree of whole person impairment, in per cent (0 if not assessed)
      `my assessment is pending because I have not reached maximum medical improvement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a medical assessor has declined to assess you because maximum medical improvement has not been reached
      `the insurer is satisfied my impairment is likely over 20%` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer is satisfied your degree of permanent impairment is likely to be more than 20%
      `the insurer is satisfied my impairment is likely over 30%` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer is satisfied your degree of permanent impairment is likely to be more than 30%
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a worker with high needs` IF
    `is a worker with high needs` `my impairment facts`
    WHERE
        `my impairment facts` MEANS `Impairment facts` WITH
            `the injury has resulted in permanent impairment`                             IS `my injury has resulted in permanent impairment`
            `the degree of permanent impairment has been assessed`                        IS `my impairment has been assessed`
            `the assessed degree of permanent impairment`                                 IS `my assessed degree of impairment`
            `an assessment is pending because maximum medical improvement is not reached` IS `my assessment is pending because I have not reached maximum medical improvement`
            `the insurer is satisfied the degree is likely to be more than 20%`           IS `the insurer is satisfied my impairment is likely over 20%`
            `the insurer is satisfied the degree is likely to be more than 30%`           IS `the insurer is satisfied my impairment is likely over 30%`

@export Am I a worker with highest needs (1987 Act s 32A)?
GIVEN `my injury has resulted in permanent impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury has left you with some permanent impairment
      `my impairment has been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the degree of your permanent impairment has been assessed (under s 65, for Division 4)
      `my assessed degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc The assessed degree of whole person impairment, in per cent (0 if not assessed)
      `my assessment is pending because I have not reached maximum medical improvement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a medical assessor has declined to assess you because maximum medical improvement has not been reached
      `the insurer is satisfied my impairment is likely over 30%` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer is satisfied your degree of permanent impairment is likely to be more than 30%
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a worker with highest needs` IF
    `is a worker with highest needs` `my impairment facts`
    WHERE
        `my impairment facts` MEANS `Impairment facts` WITH
            `the injury has resulted in permanent impairment`                             IS `my injury has resulted in permanent impairment`
            `the degree of permanent impairment has been assessed`                        IS `my impairment has been assessed`
            `the assessed degree of permanent impairment`                                 IS `my assessed degree of impairment`
            `an assessment is pending because maximum medical improvement is not reached` IS `my assessment is pending because I have not reached maximum medical improvement`
            `the insurer is satisfied the degree is likely to be more than 20%`           IS `the insurer is satisfied my impairment is likely over 30%`  -- not read for highest needs; more than 30% implies it
            `the insurer is satisfied the degree is likely to be more than 30%`           IS `the insurer is satisfied my impairment is likely over 30%`

§§ `My weekly payments (1987 Act Part 3 Division 2)`

@export Which entitlement period is this week of my weekly payments in: weeks 1-13, 14-130, 131-260, or after 260 (1987 Act s 32A)?
GIVEN `the number of this week of weekly payments` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting only the weeks for which a weekly payment has been paid or is payable (whether or not in a row), which week this is: 1 for the first
GIVETH AN `Entitlement period`
`Which entitlement period is this week in` MEANS
    `the entitlement period for week` `the number of this week of weekly payments`

@export In which week does my current entitlement period end, where my payment steps down (13), may stop (130) or stops unless my impairment is over 20% (260)?
GIVEN `the number of this week of weekly payments` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting only the weeks for which a weekly payment has been paid or is payable, which week this is: 1 for the first
GIVETH A NUMBER
`In which week does my current entitlement period end` MEANS
    `the last week of the entitlement period for week` `the number of this week of weekly payments`

@export What is the last day of incapacity my weekly payments can cover, because of my age (1987 Act s 52)?
GIVEN `the day of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the injury (ISO date)
      `the day I reach the age pension age` IS A DATE @desc The day you reach (or reached) the age at which you could get the Commonwealth age pension: Social Security Act 1991 s 23(5A)-(5D); 67 for anyone born on or after 1 January 1957 (ISO date)
      `the day I was first unable to work because of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The first day the injury made you unable to work, fully or partly (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day my weekly payments can cover because of my age` MEANS
    `the last day weekly payments may be made for under s 52` `the day of my injury` `the day I reach the age pension age` `the day I was first unable to work because of the injury`

-- Situation: weekly payments are coming up to, or past, week 130.
@export Am I entitled to weekly payments after week 130, the end of the second entitlement period (1987 Act s 38)?
GIVEN `the insurer assessed me as having no current work capacity, likely indefinitely` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has assessed you as having no current work capacity and as likely to continue indefinitely to have none
      `the insurer assessed me as having current work capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has assessed you as having current work capacity
      `I applied in writing on the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied to the insurer in writing, on the form the Authority approved, for weekly payments to continue after the second entitlement period
      `the weeks of my second entitlement period left when I applied` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of the second entitlement period were left when you applied (the application counts only if 52 or fewer)
      `the hours a week I have returned to work` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours a week you have returned to work, in any employment or self-employment (0 if none)
      `my current weekly earnings, with any deductible amount` IS A NUMBER @desc Your current weekly earnings in dollars (with any deductible amount; the Act no longer defines that term)
      `the insurer assessed me as indefinitely unable to earn more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has assessed you as, and as likely to remain indefinitely, unable to take on further work that would increase your current weekly earnings
      `I am a worker with high needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a worker with high needs (s 32A: impairment assessed at more than 20%, or likely to be, or an assessment pending)
      `the current s 38(3)(b) amount, if known` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The weekly earnings amount declared under s 82B for this financial year, if you know it; leave empty to use the $155 in the deposited text, which may be out of date
GIVETH AN `After week 130 answer`
`Am I entitled to weekly payments after week 130` MEANS
    `the s 38 entitlement`
        (`After week 130 facts` WITH
            `the insurer assessed no current work capacity, likely to continue indefinitely` IS `the insurer assessed me as having no current work capacity, likely indefinitely`
            `the insurer assessed current work capacity`                                       IS `the insurer assessed me as having current work capacity`
            `the worker applied in writing in the approved form`                              IS `I applied in writing on the approved form`
            `weeks of the second entitlement period left when the worker applied`             IS `the weeks of my second entitlement period left when I applied`
            `hours a week the worker has returned to work`                                    IS `the hours a week I have returned to work`
            `current weekly earnings, with any deductible amount`                             IS `my current weekly earnings, with any deductible amount`
            `the insurer assessed the worker as indefinitely unable to earn more`             IS `the insurer assessed me as indefinitely unable to earn more`)
        `I am a worker with high needs`
        (`the amount that applies` `the current s 38(3)(b) amount, if known` `the s 38(3)(b) earnings amount`)

-- Situation: weekly payments are coming up to, or past, 260 weeks.
@export Can my weekly payments continue after 260 weeks (1987 Act s 39)?
GIVEN `my injury has resulted in permanent impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury has left you with some permanent impairment
      `my impairment has been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the degree of your permanent impairment has been assessed (under s 65)
      `my assessed degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc The assessed degree of whole person impairment, in per cent (0 if not assessed)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my weekly payments continue after 260 weeks` IF
    `weekly payments may continue after 260 weeks`
        (`Impairment facts` WITH
            `the injury has resulted in permanent impairment`                             IS `my injury has resulted in permanent impairment`
            `the degree of permanent impairment has been assessed`                        IS `my impairment has been assessed`
            `the assessed degree of permanent impairment`                                 IS `my assessed degree of impairment`
            `an assessment is pending because maximum medical improvement is not reached` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: s 39 does not read it
            `the insurer is satisfied the degree is likely to be more than 20%`           IS FALSE  -- placeholder: s 39 does not read it
            `the insurer is satisfied the degree is likely to be more than 30%`           IS FALSE) -- placeholder: s 39 does not read it

@export How much is my weekly payment for this week of incapacity (1987 Act ss 33-39, 52; Schedule 3; Regulation cl 8AB)?
GIVEN `the day of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the injury (ISO date); injuries before 21 October 2019 are not covered
      `my class of worker` IS A `Worker class` @desc Whether you are a police officer, paramedic or firefighter, or a coal miner (not covered), or none of these
      `the number of this week of weekly payments` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting only the weeks for which a weekly payment has been paid or is payable (whether or not in a row), which week this is: 1 for the first
      `my work capacity` IS A `Work capacity` @desc As assessed: no current work capacity (unable to return to any suitable work), current work capacity (able to do some work, but to earn less than before), or no incapacity for work
      `my pre-injury average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your pre-injury average weekly earnings in dollars, as last varied on a review date (the insurer's notice states them)
      `my actual gross earnings this week` IS A NUMBER @desc What you actually earned this week, gross, in dollars (0 if nothing)
      `what I am able to earn a week in suitable employment` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly amount you are able to earn in suitable employment, in dollars, as assessed (0 if you have no current work capacity)
      `the hours a week I have returned to work` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours a week you have returned to work, in any employment or self-employment (0 if none)
      `the current maximum weekly compensation amount, if known` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The maximum weekly compensation amount the Authority declared for this period under s 82 (Division 6), if you know it; leave empty to use the $1,838.70 in s 34(1) of the deposited text, which is out of date
      `the current s 38A amount, if known` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The s 38A amount for workers with highest needs declared under s 82BA, if you know it; leave empty to use the $788.32 in the deposited text
      `my injury has resulted in permanent impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury has left you with some permanent impairment
      `my impairment has been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the degree of your permanent impairment has been assessed (under s 65)
      `my assessed degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc The assessed degree of whole person impairment, in per cent (0 if not assessed)
      `my assessment is pending because I have not reached maximum medical improvement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a medical assessor has declined to assess you because maximum medical improvement has not been reached
      `the insurer is satisfied my impairment is likely over 30%` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer is satisfied your degree of permanent impairment is likely to be more than 30%
      `I am entitled to weekly payments after week 130` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only after week 130: whether s 38 continues your payments (ask the s 38 question)
      `the day I reach the age pension age` IS A DATE @desc The day you reach (or reached) the Commonwealth age pension age (Social Security Act 1991 s 23(5A)-(5D); 67 for anyone born on or after 1 January 1957) (ISO date)
      `the day I was first unable to work because of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The first day the injury made you unable to work, fully or partly (ISO date)
      `a day in this week of incapacity` IS A DATE @desc A day of incapacity in the week you are asking about (ISO date)
GIVETH A `Weekly payment`
`How much is my weekly payment this week` MEANS
    `the weekly payment` (`the scope check` `the day of my injury` `my class of worker`)
        (`Weekly facts` WITH
            `which week of weekly payments this is`                              IS `the number of this week of weekly payments`
            `the work capacity`                                                  IS `my work capacity`
            `the pre-injury average weekly earnings`                             IS `my pre-injury average weekly earnings`
            `the current weekly earnings`                                        IS `the current weekly earnings` `my actual gross earnings this week` `what I am able to earn a week in suitable employment`
            `hours a week the worker has returned to work`                       IS `the hours a week I have returned to work`
            `the maximum weekly compensation amount`                             IS `the amount that applies` `the current maximum weekly compensation amount, if known` `the maximum weekly compensation amount (s 34(1))`
            `the s 38A amount`                                                   IS `the amount that applies` `the current s 38A amount, if known` `the s 38A amount for a worker with highest needs`
            `a worker with highest needs`                                        IS `is a worker with highest needs` `my impairment facts`
            `the worker is entitled after the second entitlement period under s 38` IS `I am entitled to weekly payments after week 130`
            `weekly payments may continue after 260 weeks under s 39(2)`        IS `weekly payments may continue after 260 weeks` `my impairment facts`
            `the day of the incapacity`                                          IS `a day in this week of incapacity`
            `the last day weekly payments may be made for under s 52`            IS `the last day weekly payments may be made for under s 52` `the day of my injury` `the day I reach the age pension age` `the day I was first unable to work because of the injury`)
    WHERE
        `my impairment facts` MEANS `Impairment facts` WITH
            `the injury has resulted in permanent impairment`                             IS `my injury has resulted in permanent impairment`
            `the degree of permanent impairment has been assessed`                        IS `my impairment has been assessed`
            `the assessed degree of permanent impairment`                                 IS `my assessed degree of impairment`
            `an assessment is pending because maximum medical improvement is not reached` IS `my assessment is pending because I have not reached maximum medical improvement`
            `the insurer is satisfied the degree is likely to be more than 20%`           IS `the insurer is satisfied my impairment is likely over 30%`  -- not read for highest needs or s 39
            `the insurer is satisfied the degree is likely to be more than 30%`           IS `the insurer is satisfied my impairment is likely over 30%`

§§ `My medical expenses (1987 Act s 59A)`

@export For how long will compensation for my medical and related treatment be paid (1987 Act s 59A)?
GIVEN `the day of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the injury (ISO date); injuries before 21 October 2019 are not covered
      `my class of worker` IS A `Worker class` @desc Whether you are a police officer, paramedic or firefighter, or a coal miner (not covered), or none of these
      `the kind of treatment` IS A `Treatment kind` @desc The kind of treatment, service or assistance you are asking about
      `the surgery follows earlier surgery on the same part of my body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For surgery: whether it is directly consequential on earlier surgery and affects a part of the body that surgery affected
      `the insurer approved the surgery within 2 years of approving the earlier one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For surgery: whether the insurer approved it within 2 years after approving the earlier surgery (or later, after a dispute that arose within those 2 years)
      `I am a worker with high needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a worker with high needs (s 32A: impairment assessed at more than 20%, or likely to be, or an assessment pending)
      `my impairment has been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the degree of your permanent impairment has been assessed (under s 65)
      `my assessed degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc The assessed degree of whole person impairment, in per cent (0 if not assessed)
      `I have had weekly payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether weekly payments are or have been paid or payable to you for the injury
      `my weekly payments are still payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether weekly payments are still payable to you
      `the day I first made my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day your claim for compensation for the injury was first made (ISO date)
      `the day my weekly payments stopped being payable` IS A DATE @desc If they have stopped, the day weekly payments ceased to be payable (otherwise any date)
GIVETH A `Medical compensation period`
`For how long will my medical expenses be paid` MEANS
    `the medical compensation period, within scope` (`the scope check` `the day of my injury` `my class of worker`) `my medical facts`
    WHERE
        `my medical facts` MEANS `Medical facts` WITH
            `the kind of treatment`                                                      IS `the kind of treatment`
            `the surgery is directly consequential on earlier surgery and affects the same part of the body` IS `the surgery follows earlier surgery on the same part of my body`
            `the insurer approved it within 2 years after approving the earlier surgery, or later on a dispute raised within them` IS `the insurer approved the surgery within 2 years of approving the earlier one`
            `a worker with high needs`                                                   IS `I am a worker with high needs`
            `the degree of permanent impairment has been assessed`                       IS `my impairment has been assessed`
            `the assessed degree of permanent impairment`                                IS `my assessed degree of impairment`
            `weekly payments are or have been paid or payable`                           IS `I have had weekly payments`
            `weekly payments are still payable`                                          IS `my weekly payments are still payable`
            `the day the claim was first made`                                           IS `the day I first made my claim`
            `the day weekly payments ceased to be payable`                               IS `the day my weekly payments stopped being payable`

@export Will compensation be paid for treatment I get on this day (1987 Act s 59A(1), (3))?
GIVEN `the day of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the injury (ISO date); injuries before 21 October 2019 are not covered
      `my class of worker` IS A `Worker class` @desc Whether you are a police officer, paramedic or firefighter, or a coal miner (not covered), or none of these
      `the kind of treatment` IS A `Treatment kind` @desc The kind of treatment, service or assistance you are asking about
      `the surgery follows earlier surgery on the same part of my body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For surgery: whether it is directly consequential on earlier surgery and affects a part of the body that surgery affected
      `the insurer approved the surgery within 2 years of approving the earlier one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For surgery: whether the insurer approved it within 2 years after approving the earlier surgery (or later, after a dispute that arose within those 2 years)
      `I am a worker with high needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a worker with high needs (s 32A: impairment assessed at more than 20%, or likely to be, or an assessment pending)
      `my impairment has been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the degree of your permanent impairment has been assessed (under s 65)
      `my assessed degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc The assessed degree of whole person impairment, in per cent (0 if not assessed)
      `I have had weekly payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether weekly payments are or have been paid or payable to you for the injury
      `my weekly payments are still payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether weekly payments are still payable to you
      `the day I first made my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day your claim for compensation for the injury was first made (ISO date)
      `the day my weekly payments stopped being payable` IS A DATE @desc If they have stopped, the day weekly payments ceased to be payable (otherwise any date)
      `the day of the treatment` IS A DATE @desc The day the treatment, service or assistance is given (ISO date)
      `weekly payments are payable to me for that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether weekly payments are payable to you for that day (for example, because they started again)
GIVETH A `Treatment day answer`
`Will my treatment on this day be paid for` MEANS
    `medical compensation for treatment on the day`
        (`For how long will my medical expenses be paid` `the day of my injury` `my class of worker` `the kind of treatment` `the surgery follows earlier surgery on the same part of my body` `the insurer approved the surgery within 2 years of approving the earlier one` `I am a worker with high needs` `my impairment has been assessed` `my assessed degree of impairment` `I have had weekly payments` `my weekly payments are still payable` `the day I first made my claim` `the day my weekly payments stopped being payable`)
        `the day of the treatment`
        `weekly payments are payable to me for that day`

§§ `My lump sum for permanent impairment (1987 Act s 66)`

-- Situation: the worker's permanent impairment has been assessed.
@export What lump sum is payable for my permanent impairment (1987 Act s 66)?
GIVEN `the day of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the injury (ISO date); injuries before 21 October 2019 are not covered
      `my class of worker` IS A `Worker class` @desc Whether you are a police officer, paramedic or firefighter, or a coal miner (not covered), or none of these
      `my assessed degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc The degree of permanent impairment from the injury, in per cent, as assessed under s 65
      `the per cent of my impairment that is of my back` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the impairment is of the back, in per cent of the whole (0 if none, 100 if all)
      `I have already claimed permanent impairment compensation for this injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a claim for permanent impairment compensation has already been made for the injury (only one is allowed)
      `the current amount for my band, if known` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The amount the Authority declared under s 82F for your band of impairment for the financial year of the injury, if you know it; leave empty to use the amount in s 66(2) of the deposited text
GIVETH A `Permanent impairment answer`
`What lump sum is payable for my permanent impairment` MEANS
    `the permanent impairment compensation` (`the scope check` `the day of my injury` `my class of worker`) `my assessed degree of impairment` `the per cent of my impairment that is of my back` `I have already claimed permanent impairment compensation for this injury` `the current amount for my band, if known`

§§ `If the worker has died (the dependants' questions)`

-- Situation: the worker died as a result of the injury. These questions are asked by the dependants.
@export What lump sum death benefit is payable, and to whom (1987 Act s 25(1)(a), (4); s 29)?
GIVEN `the day the worker died` IS A DATE @desc The day of the worker's death (ISO date); deaths before 21 October 2019 are not covered
      `the number of dependants` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people were wholly or partly dependent on the worker for support (0 if none)
      `the lump sum in force at the date of death, if known` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The lump sum death benefit declared under Division 6 (s 82) for the date of death, if you know it; leave empty to use the $750,000 in s 25(1)(a) of the deposited text
GIVETH A `Death benefit answer`
`What lump sum death benefit is payable` MEANS
    `the death benefit` (`the death scope check` `the day the worker died`) (`the amount that applies` `the lump sum in force at the date of death, if known` `the lump sum death benefit (s 25(1)(a))`) `the number of dependants`

@export Is a weekly payment payable for this child of the worker this week, and how much (1987 Act s 25(1)(b), (2), (5))?
GIVEN `the day the worker died` IS A DATE @desc The day of the worker's death (ISO date); deaths before 21 October 2019 are not covered
      `the child was dependent on the worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child (or stepchild, or a child the worker stood in the place of a parent to) was wholly or partly dependent on the worker for support
      `the child's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The child's age this week, in whole years
      `the child is a full-time student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is in full-time education at a school, college or university
      `the weekly amount in force, if known` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The weekly amount for a dependent child declared under Division 6, if you know it; leave empty to use the $66.60 in s 25(1)(b) of the deposited text
GIVETH AN `Amount answer`
`Is a weekly payment payable for this child` MEANS
    `the weekly payment for the child` (`the death scope check` `the day the worker died`) (`the amount that applies` `the weekly amount in force, if known` `the weekly payment for each dependent child (s 25(1)(b))`) (`a weekly payment is payable for the child` `the child was dependent on the worker` `the child's age` `the child is a full-time student`)

@export How much of the funeral expenses must the employer pay (1987 Act s 26)?
GIVEN `the day the worker died` IS A DATE @desc The day of the worker's death (ISO date); deaths before 21 October 2019 are not covered
      `the reasonable funeral expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc The reasonable funeral expenses, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount answer`
`How much of the funeral expenses must be paid` MEANS
    `the funeral expenses answer` (`the death scope check` `the day the worker died`) `the reasonable funeral expenses`

§§ `Telling my employer and making my claim (1998 Act ss 44, 254, 261)`

@export Can I still recover compensation, given when I told my employer about the injury (1998 Act s 254)?
GIVEN `I told my employer as soon as possible after the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave your employer notice of the injury as soon as possible after it happened (orally or in writing; s 44(1) also requires it)
      `I told my employer before I voluntarily left that job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the notice before you voluntarily left the job you had when injured (true if you are still there)
      `the special circumstance` IS A `Special circumstance` @desc If notice was late or missing, the special circumstance that applies (s 254(3)-(4)); it must be found in proceedings
GIVETH A `Notice of injury answer`
`Can I still recover compensation given my notice of injury` MEANS
    `the notice of injury position` `I told my employer as soon as possible after the injury` `I told my employer before I voluntarily left that job` `the special circumstance`

@export By what day must I make my claim for compensation (1998 Act s 261(1), (6), (7))?
GIVEN `the day of the injury or death` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury happened, or for a claim for a death, the day of the death (ISO date)
      `the day I first became aware of it` IS A DATE @desc The day you first became aware you had been injured (or, for a death, that it resulted from the injury); the same day if at once (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I make my claim` MEANS
    `months after` 6 (`the day time runs from under s 261(6), (7)` `the day of the injury or death` `the day I first became aware of it`)

@export Is my claim in time, or does an exception keep it alive (1998 Act s 261)?
GIVEN `my claim is for a death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for compensation for the worker's death
      `the day of the injury or death` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury happened, or for a claim for a death, the day of the death (ISO date)
      `the day I first became aware of it` IS A DATE @desc The day you first became aware you had been injured (or, for a death, that it resulted from the injury); the same day if at once (ISO date)
      `the day I made the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim was made (any claim for compensation for the injury counts, s 261(3)) (ISO date)
      `the worker's own claim was in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a death claim: whether the worker made a claim within time for the injury that caused the death
      `the lateness is found to come from a reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is found that the late claim was due to ignorance, mistake, absence from the State or other reasonable cause
      `the injury caused death or serious and permanent disablement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury resulted in death or serious and permanent disablement
      `the insurer decided to accept my late claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has determined to accept the claim although it is late
      `the Authority approved the insurer accepting it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a claim made more than 3 years after: whether the State Insurance Regulatory Authority approved the insurer's acceptance
GIVETH A `Claim time answer`
`Is my claim in time` MEANS
    `the claim time position`
        (`Claim time facts` WITH
            `the claim is for compensation for a death`                                 IS `my claim is for a death`
            `the day time runs from`                                                    IS `the day time runs from under s 261(6), (7)` `the day of the injury or death` `the day I first became aware of it`
            `the day the claim was made`                                                IS `the day I made the claim`
            `the worker made a claim within time for the injury that caused the death` IS `the worker's own claim was in time`
            `the lateness is found to come from ignorance, mistake, absence from the State or other reasonable cause` IS `the lateness is found to come from a reasonable cause`
            `the injury resulted in death or serious and permanent disablement`         IS `the injury caused death or serious and permanent disablement`
            `the insurer has determined to accept the claim`                            IS `the insurer decided to accept my late claim`
            `the Authority approved the insurer's acceptance`                           IS `the Authority approved the insurer accepting it`)

§§ `Deadlines my employer and the insurer must meet (1998 Act ss 264, 267, 268, 274)`

@export Has my employer missed its 7-day deadline to forward my claim to its insurer (1998 Act s 264(1))?
GIVEN `my employer is a self-insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer is a licensed self-insurer (it then has no insurer to forward to)
      `the day my employer received my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer received your claim or document (ISO date)
      `my employer has forwarded it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has forwarded it to its insurer
      `the day my employer forwarded it` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it did (otherwise any date)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (ISO date)
GIVETH A `Deadline answer`
`Has my employer missed the deadline to forward my claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day to forward the claim by, if any` `my employer is a self-insurer` `the day my employer received my claim`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `no such duty`
    WHEN JUST `the last day` THEN `the deadline position` `the last day` `my employer has forwarded it` `the day my employer forwarded it` `today`

@export Has the insurer missed its 7-day deadline to start provisional weekly payments, or to tell me in writing of its reasonable excuse (1998 Act ss 267, 268)?
GIVEN `the day the insurer was first notified of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day of the initial notification of your injury to the insurer, by you, your employer or someone for either (s 266) (ISO date)
      `my provisional weekly payments have started` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has started provisional weekly payments
      `the day my payments started` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day they started (otherwise any date)
      `the insurer gave me written notice of a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer gave you written notice that it has a reasonable excuse for not starting them
      `the day I got that notice` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it was given (otherwise any date)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (ISO date)
GIVETH A `Deadline answer`
`Has the insurer missed its 7-day deadline` MEANS
    `the position under ss 267 and 268` `the day the insurer was first notified of my injury` `my provisional weekly payments have started` `the day my payments started` `the insurer gave me written notice of a reasonable excuse` `the day I got that notice` `today`

@export Has the insurer missed its deadline to decide my claim for weekly payments (1998 Act s 274)?
GIVEN `the day I made my claim for weekly payments` IS A DATE @desc The day your claim for weekly payments was made (a claim forwarded by your employer counts as made on the insurer) (ISO date)
      `the weeks the insurer accepted liability provisionally for` IS A NUMBER @desc If the insurer accepted liability provisionally (s 274(2), or provisional payments under s 267), for how many weeks (0 if not)
      `the day the provisional acceptance of my claim began` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it began (otherwise any date)
      `the insurer has decided my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has accepted liability and started weekly payments, or disputed liability
      `the day the insurer decided` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day (otherwise any date)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (ISO date)
GIVETH A `Deadline answer`
`Has the insurer missed its deadline to decide my weekly payments claim` MEANS
    `the deadline position` (`the day by which the claim for weekly payments must be determined` `the day I made my claim for weekly payments` `the weeks the insurer accepted liability provisionally for` `the day the provisional acceptance of my claim began`) `the insurer has decided my claim` `the day the insurer decided` `today`

§§ `Returning to work (1998 Act ss 48, 48A, 49)`

-- Situation: the worker is able to do some work.
@export Must my employer give me suitable work (1998 Act s 49)?
GIVEN `I am able to return to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are able to return to work, full-time or part-time, in your old job or another
      `I have asked my employer for suitable work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have asked your employer (the one liable to compensate you) to provide suitable employment
      `it is not reasonably practicable for my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is not reasonably practicable for your employer to provide it
      `I left that job voluntarily after the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you voluntarily left that employer after the injury
      `my employer ended my job after the injury, not because the injury made me unfit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer terminated your employment after the injury for some reason other than unfitness from the injury
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer give me suitable work` IF
    `the employer must provide suitable employment`
        (`Suitable work facts` WITH
            `the worker is able to return to work`                                         IS `I am able to return to work`
            `the worker has asked the employer for suitable employment`                     IS `I have asked my employer for suitable work`
            `it is not reasonably practicable to provide it`                               IS `it is not reasonably practicable for my employer`
            `the worker voluntarily left the employment after the injury`                  IS `I left that job voluntarily after the injury`
            `the employer ended the employment after the injury, not for unfitness from the injury` IS `my employer ended my job after the injury, not because the injury made me unfit`)

-- Situation: the insurer has given the worker a notice under s 48A(2).
@export The insurer gave me a notice about my return to work obligations: what can it do, and from when (1998 Act ss 48, 48A)?
GIVEN `the day I got the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer gave you the written notice (ISO date)
      `the date in the notice` IS A DATE @desc The date from which the notice says your weekly payments will be suspended (ISO date)
      `the notice gives the reason, my obligation and the consequences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice states the reason for it, the s 48 obligation you must comply with, and the consequences of not complying
      `I have complied with the obligation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have complied with the obligation the notice specifies
      `the day I complied` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day you complied (otherwise any date)
      `I had 2 notices without a suspension, or a suspension, in the 12 months before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the 12 months before this notice, you were given 2 such notices without a suspension following, or had weekly payments suspended once
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (ISO date)
GIVETH A `Section 48A answer`
`What can the insurer do after its return to work notice` MEANS
    `what the insurer may do under s 48A`
        (`Section 48A facts` WITH
            `the day the notice was given`                                           IS `the day I got the notice`
            `the date specified in the notice`                                       IS `the date in the notice`
            `the notice states the reason, the obligation and the consequences`     IS `the notice gives the reason, my obligation and the consequences`
            `the worker has complied with the obligation in the notice`             IS `I have complied with the obligation`
            `the day the worker complied`                                            IS `the day I complied`
            `in the 12 months before the notice: 2 notices without a suspension, or 1 suspension` IS `I had 2 notices without a suspension, or a suspension, in the 12 months before`
            `the day asked about`                                                    IS `today`)
